CommitDate: Fri Oct 23 09:30:06 2026 +0800

    [Refactor][Worker] move speculative decoding into v1 worker (#19371)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    Move the Model Runner V1 speculative decoding implementation from
    vllm_ascend/spec_decode/ to vllm_ascend/worker/v1/spec_decode/ to make
    its ownership explicit.
    Keep shared helpers outside the V1 directory:
    - Extract token-count and sequence-length correction helpers, together
    with PREPARE_INPUTS_BLOCK_SIZE, into worker/spec_decode_utils.py.
    - Move DSpark auxiliary-layer utilities into worker/dspark_utils.py.
    Update affected imports, profiling symbols, test mock targets, and
    source regression paths. Relocate the corresponding shared utility tests
    to tests/ut/worker/. This keeps shared callers from depending on
    V1-specific modules for these utilities.
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No changes to inference behavior, configuration, or model outputs are
    intended. Internal Python import paths change as part of the module
    reorganization.
    ### How was this patch tested?
    - Shared speculative decoding and DSpark utility tests: 23 passed.
    - Step3.5 source regression tests: 3 passed.
    - Ruff checks, formatting, and git diff --check passed.
    - PR CI checks passed, including E2E.
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    - [x] Boundary / edge-case coverage: Preserved existing coverage for the
    relocated helpers, including new requests, prefills, rejected drafts,
    and auxiliary-layer validation.
    - [x] Regression test: Updated existing regression tests and source
    paths to follow the relocated modules.
    - [x] Error / failure path coverage: Preserved existing validation and
    failure-path tests; no new error-handling behavior was introduced.
    - [x] Meaningful & reliable tests: Retained behavioral assertions for
    the moved utilities and updated affected imports and mock targets.
    - [x] Performance impact: No performance-sensitive algorithm changes are
    intended; no performance benchmarks were added.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: shenyunyang <15713002151@163.com>

